<div class="callout"><p class="callout-title">À retenir</p><p>“Work” is uncountable: <em>I have a lot of work</em>. “Job” is countable: <em>She has two jobs</em>.</p></div>$html$);
<div class="callout"><p class="callout-title">Writing a letter of application</p><ol><li>Your address and the date (top right), the employer’s address (left).</li><li>Dear Sir / Dear Madam (or Dear Mr Diallo).</li><li>Paragraph 1: the job you are applying for and where you saw the advertisement.</li><li>Paragraph 2: your qualifications and experience.</li><li>Paragraph 3: why you want the job; your availability for an interview.</li><li>Yours faithfully (if you began with Dear Sir) or Yours sincerely (with a name), then your signature.</li></ol></div>$html$);
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Word</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>poverty / poor</td><td>la pauvreté / pauvre</td></tr><tr><td>wealth / wealthy</td><td>la richesse / riche</td></tr><tr><td>sustainable development</td><td>développement durable</td></tr><tr><td>cash crops</td><td>cultures de rente</td></tr><tr><td>to export / to import</td><td>exporter / importer</td></tr><tr><td>the consumer society</td><td>la société de consommation</td></tr></tbody></table>$html$);
